{
  "text": " That's not three, said Arnwen. Now it's one, and whatever tally cuts, Kiva held her wet right hand against her coat, and in the third, if it's close, we try the hurdle again, with our wrists and our elbows, and no fingers at all. Prue was looking at her own hands, at the crooks of her elbows. She lifted her forearms together in front of her, as a girl lifts them to carry a basket of washing on her arms, and looked at the gap between them.",
